speechtext:
The House resumed from Tuesday, April 11, consideration of the motion of Mr. Richardson for an address to Her Excellency the Governor General in reply to her Speech of the opening of the session; and on the amendment of Mr. Foster:
That the following be added to the Address:
"This House regrets that Your Excellency's advisors have failed to recognize the importance of agriculture to Canada's economy:
(1)	by only making a three-line reference to agriculture in the Speech from the Throne implying that farmers are a drain on the national treasury;
The Address-Mr Bevilacqua
(2)	by removing oats from the jurisdiction of the Canadian Wheat Board without consulting with, or obtaining the approval of, the major farm organizations thereby adding to concerns that the Board will eventually be dismantled;
(3)	by taking a position in the Free Trade negotiations which will lead to a weakening, if not the destruction, of Canada's orderly marketing systems in the grain, poultry, dairy and horticultural sectors and by not providing adequate adjustment programs as evidenced by the de Grandpre Report;
(4)	by failing to commence negotiations with the U.S. on an agricultural subsidy code so that farmers will not face U.S. countervail at the whim of U.S. lobby groups such as is now threatening Canada's pork producers;
(5)	by undermining the viability of the beef industry by allowing increasing amounts of "no roll" (ungraded) beef into Canada from the U.S.; and
(6)	by not providing any new initiatives through the Farm Credit Corporation to cope with the farm debt crisis and high interest rates."
